All three hinge on the **same obstruction**: they need continuity of an ℝ≥0∞-valued conditional-risk integral, but the frozen `ForMathlib/MeasurableArgmin.exists_measurable_argmin` brick demands *full* continuity (its own docstring notes the LSC weakening is not done), and for an unbounded convex loss the objective genuinely jumps to `∞` at its finiteness boundary. No side hypothesis closes them without laundering the analytic core, so the pre-authorized hypothesis additions do **not** apply cleanly.

